 "date": "2026-10-08",
 "scope": "RTCW SP and MP world and entity collision: retail WolfSP.exe 1.32 and WolfMP.exe 1.41 dedicated servers against fnTech3, one synthetic native game module per mode",
 "baseCommit": "84bcf66bcbd3834fb388d48f6f3025d8cdfb2043",
 "build": "fntech3.ded.exe built from baseCommit plus this change and the RTCW area-portal close (2026-10-08-rtcw-area-portals.md), which no trace here reaches",
 "platform": "Windows 11, x86 MSVC builds; dedicated servers on loopback, private desktop",
 "installation": "Steam Return to Castle Wolfenstein: WolfSP.exe \"Wolf 1.32\", WolfMP.exe \"Wolf 1.4-MP\"; game directory Main; read only",
 "module": {
  "source": ".tmp/q3-trace/q3trace_module.c (not committed), built with GAME_RTCWSP or GAME_RTCWMP",
  "abi": "dllEntry/vmMain; SP imports G_TRACE 26, G_POINT_CONTENTS 27, G_LINKENTITY 32, G_ENTITIES_IN_BOX 34, G_TRACECAPSULE 45; MP G_TRACE 25, G_POINT_CONTENTS 26, G_LINKENTITY 31, G_ENTITIES_IN_BOX 33, G_TRACECAPSULE 44 (code/compat/rtcw_module_calls.def); sharedEntity_t 680 bytes (SP) and 684 (MP), r.linked at 576, r.svFlags at 584; 56-byte trace_t",
  "loading": "MP: WolfMP.exe's Sys_LoadDll (0x445240) tries fs_basepath/fs_game then fs_basepath/main, so a scratch fs_basepath holds main/qagame_mp_x86.dll and the installation is fs_cdpath. SP: WolfSP.exe's Sys_LoadDll (0x441c10) first loads the bare name, which finds the installation's own qagamex86.dll beside the executable; under cdb that result is set to none as it returns (bp 0x441cb4 \"r eax=0; gc\"), nothing patched, and the engine goes on to fs_cdpath/main. fnTech3: fs_homepath/main. All dedicated 1, sv_pure 0, bot_enable 0",
  "worldBattery": "seeded LCG (seed 20261008); four hulls (point, player box, random box up to 32, player box as a capsule trace) x three masks (1, 0x2010001, -1) x three shapes (long, vertical drop, short <=48), 300 of each shape; 1,500 point contents; pass entity 1023",
  "entityBattery": "every brush model *k (up to 32) on entity 300+k, contents 1, moved by (8k,-4k,2k), even k turned; link flags and bounds; 90 traces around each; 200 EntitiesInBox queries; a player-sized box entity (contents body) traced 300 times with box and capsule hulls; then the same entity flagged SVF_CAPSULE (0x200) traced 600 times with point, box and capsule hulls, one in four a position test, and 200 point contents around it"
 },
 "retailRules": {
  "brushAllSolidContents": "CM_TraceThroughBrush writes no contents when the sweep starts and ends inside the brush (WolfSP.exe 0x4194bd..0x4194f1, WolfMP.exe 0x41bfdd..0x41c011)",
  "curvePositionContents": "CM_TestInLeaf sets fraction 0, startsolid and allsolid on a curve position hit, no contents (WolfSP.exe 0x418b8d..0x418ba2, WolfMP.exe 0x41b6ad..0x41b6c2)",
  "mpFacetSizes": "BaseWindingForPlane reaches 8192 units (WolfMP.exe 0x419ae8..0x419b30), WindingBounds starts from +-99999 (0x4198e9), CM_ValidateFacet keeps a facet no wider than 4096 on any axis and checks nothing else (0x4185d7..0x4185f0)",
  "spFacetSizes": "BaseWindingForPlane reaches 131072 units (WolfSP.exe 0x416fd8..0x417020), WindingBounds starts from +-131072 (0x416dd9), CM_ValidateFacet applies Quake III three checks at 131072 (0x415987..0x4159bf)",
  "mpPositionTest": "CM_PositionTestInPatchCollide (WolfMP.exe 0x418f00): bounds test, then every plane classified front/back/straddling by the box extent, inside a facet whose surface plane straddles and whose borders straddle or match borderInward; ignores the capsule",
  "spPositionTest": "Quake III 1.32's capsule-aware test (WolfSP.exe 0x4162d0: a point is never inside)",
  "mpPointGuard": "CM_TracePointThroughPatchCollide returns only when cm_playerCurveClip is 0 and the trace is not a point (WolfMP.exe 0x41860a..0x418629); SP returns when either holds (0x4159da..0x4159fd)",
  "spTempModels": "CM_Trace turns the capsule off and traces the box leaf for handle 0x1ff or 0x1fe (WolfSP.exe 0x41a77b..0x41a7ae, 0x41a86a..0x41a89a); CM_TempBoxModel builds the box planes for a capsule too and returns capsule ? 0x1fe : 0x1ff (0x41386e..0x41387b). MP keeps the capsule routines (0x41d291..0x41d2c7)",
  "areaPortalClose": "CM_AdjustAreaPortalState skips the decrement when the count is zero and floods as after any close (WolfSP.exe 0x418489..0x41849a, WolfMP.exe 0x41afa9..0x41afba)"
 },
